.TH TPM2SH 1 "2025-11-22" "tpm2sh 0.15.23" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tpm2sh \- a command-line tool for accessing TPM 2.0 devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tpm2sh
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fICOMMAND-OPTIONS\fR] [\fIARGUMENTS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tpm2sh
is a command-line tool for accessing TPM 2.0 devices.
.P
.B tpm2sh
provides a virtual memory manager for sharing key, sealed object,
and session resources across multiple commands. It is the primary mechanism for
managing and accessing transient TPM objects, which exist only as long as the
application is running.
.P
The physical memory of a TPM chip is referenced with the 'tpm:' prefix, and virtual
memory with the 'vtpm:' prefix. For example, 'tpm:81000001' references a persistent
handle in physical memory, while 'vtpm:80000000' might reference a transient
key loaded into the virtual memory cache.
.P
The cache automatically invalidates and resets on reboot, requiring very
little management from the user.
.P
.B tpm2sh
provides 'convert' and 'load' subcommands for loading DER or PEM
encoded internal and external keys. The tool uses the TPMKey ASN.1 format as
the native output format when creating new TPM keys.
It supports PKCS#1, PKCS#8, and SEC1 formats for external keys.
.P
Several commands, such as
.BR create ,
.BR create-primary ,
and
.BR convert ,
accept a
.BR --policy " option to specify an inline authorization policy expression."

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -d, --device=\fI<DEVICE>\fR
Device file [default: /dev/tpmrm0].
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print help.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Print version.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B algorithm
Lists available algorithms supported by the chip.
.TP
.B cache
Lists cached TPM objects.
.TP
.B convert
Convert external keys to TPM keys.
.TP
.B create
Creates a secondary key or a sealed data object.
.TP
.B create-primary
Creates a new primary key in a specified hierarchy.
.TP
.B delete
Deletes active and cached objects.
.TP
.B evict
Create persistent object from transient object.
.TP
.B help
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s).
.TP
.B load
Loads a PEM or DER TPMKey file to cache. If the TPMKey file does not include
a parent public area, a parent handle must be supplied with
.BR -P " or " --parent .
.TP
.B memory
Lists objects inside TPM memory or inspects a single handle.
.TP
.B pcr-event
Extends a PCR with an event.
.TP
.B reset-lock
Resets the dictionary attack lockout counter.
.TP
.B return-code
Prints a TPM return code in human-readable format.
.TP
.B unseal
Retrieves data from a sealed data object.

.SH LOAD OPTIONS
.TP
.B -P, --parent=\fI<tpm:HANDLE|vtpm:HANDLE>\fR
Parent handle to use when the TPMKey file does not include the parent public area.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TPM2SH_CACHE_PATH
Overrides the default per-user cache directory used to store virtual TPM
state. When unset, a system-appropriate per-user cache directory is used.

